  "item": [
    {
      "id": "554e3152-7e65-481f-a90b-ac1415ec0a88",
      "name": "scopes",
      "description": {
        "content": "Scopes define the type of resource and the operation that you can perform with the access token you bear. For example, `scans:create` means that the bearer of the token with this scope can create scans via the API.\n\nFor each endpoint, we indicate the scope required to perform an operation under **Authorizations**.\n\nWe also offer helper endpoints that allow you to determine what the allowed scopes for your access token are in the context of a specific API resource.\n\n[![Run in Postman](https://run.pstmn.io/button.svg)](https://god.gw.postman.com/run-collection/9829310-54d0d8f3-0cc0-42c3-8eee-2eb66e1ea835?action=collection%2Ffork&collection-url=entityId%3D9829310-54d0d8f3-0cc0-42c3-8eee-2eb66e1ea835%26entityType%3Dcollection%26workspaceId%3Da63f69cc-5c31-4f2b-8d28-b647f83b9e97)\n",
        "type": "text/plain"
      },
